PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus remains completely unanimous across all eight participants in support of Choice C.
- The decisive factor is that single-cell RT-PCR amplifies immunoglobulin chains from any present B cell regardless of antigen specificity, meaning the lack of amplicons reflects physical absence of B cells rather than non-specific binding (ruling out Choice B).
- The brief 40-minute incubation followed by 30 minutes on ice disrupts active cytoskeletal and adhesion dynamics, causing fragile cell conjugates to dissociate under fluidic shear forces during sorting so they fail to persist into the wells.
- Distractors D and E are conclusively eliminated due to factual inaccuracy (referencing TCR chains) and biochemical impossibility (picogram RNA levels cannot overwhelm reverse transcriptase), respectively.
}

