4.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Unanimous consensus firmly supports Choice C based on molecular and biophysical mechanisms.
- Universal BCR RT-PCR primers amplify immunoglobulin heavy and light chains from any mature B cell; failure to amplify in 91 of 95 wells indicates the physical absence of B cells in those wells, ruling out non-specific binding (Choice B).
- The brief 40-minute co-culture followed by 30 minutes on ice prevents the cytoskeletal stabilization and integrin clustering necessary for conjugates to withstand hydrodynamic shear stress in the sorter nozzle, leading to conjugate dissociation prior to deposition into the RT buffer (Choice C).
- Distractors are conclusively ruled out: Choice A ignores the temperature-dependent destabilization, Choice D incorrectly refers to T-cell receptor alpha/beta chains, and Choice E is invalid because picogram quantities of single-cell RNA cannot overwhelm the microgram capacity of SuperScript III.
}

