PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The panel remains unanimous in selecting Choice C, supported by molecular and biophysical mechanisms.
- PCR amplification of BCR heavy and light chains depends on single-cell presence rather than antigen specificity; the failure to amplify in 91 of 95 wells indicates the physical absence of B cells in the wells, directly ruling out Choice B.
- The brief 40-minute incubation followed by cold staining on ice prevents the formation of stable, shear-resistant conjugates, causing fragile doublets to dissociate under sorting shear forces and fail to persist into collection plates.
- Distractors A, D, and E remain eliminated due to incompleteness, factual inaccuracies regarding TCR chains, and biochemical implausibility of RNA saturation, respectively.
}

